# {{name}} server API

The contract between the app (`../src/lib.rs`) and this server
(`src/app.js`). Change the three together.

```
Base URL   http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}   (development)
Content    application/json
```

## Every request

- `X-Device-Id`: who is asking, 8 to 64 characters of `A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -`.
  The app sends its installation id. Not needed for `/v1/health`.
- `Authorization: Bearer <token>`: only when the server was started with
  `APP_TOKEN`. Not needed for `/v1/health`.
- A device may make `RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE` requests a minute (60 unless
  set). Beyond that the answer is `429` with `Retry-After` in seconds.

## Errors

Every error is JSON with a code for programs and a sentence for people:

```json
{"error": {"code": "bad_request", "message": "The body must be a JSON object."}}
```

| Status | Code | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 400 | `bad_request` | A missing or malformed device id, body or field |
| 401 | `unauthorized` | A token is required and was missing or wrong |
| 404 | `not_found` | No such address |
| 405 | `method_not_allowed` | The address exists, the method does not |
| 413 | `too_large` | A body over 16 KB |
| 429 | `rate_limited` | Too many requests this minute |
| 500 | `internal_error` | A fault in the server; the log has it |

## `GET /v1/health`

Whether the server is up. **200** `{"ok": true}`.

## `POST /v1/hello`

The example resource: says hello and counts how often this device has.

```json
{"name": "Ada"}
```

`name` is optional, a string of at most 40 characters. **200**

```json
{"message": "Hello, Ada. That is 3 from this phone.", "count": 3}
```

## `GET /v1/hello`

**200** `{"count": 3}`: how often this device has said hello.

The count is kept in memory and starts again when the server restarts.
